      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "This construction makes each line contain an assertion and its",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "reason. The commentator would make the third line only a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "mere assertion without reason assigned.—Sragdharâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. CVII.—On the second line Râmarshi says तस्य अर्धस्य पञ्चाशद्व-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "र्षाणां परस्य अर्धस्य पञ्चविंशतिवर्षाणामित्यर्थः अर्धं सार्धद्वादशवर्षाणि पुनः सार्धद्वादशवर्षा-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "णीत्यर्थः....शेषमुर्वरितमायुः पञ्चविंशतिपरिमितवर्षमित्यर्थः. This is not quite",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "clear. I suggest the following : तस्य (आयुषः) परस्य (रात्रिगतार्धेतरस्य)",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "अर्धस्य अपरमर्धम्. The commentary says ततोनन्तरं तस्य पञ्चाशत अ (sic)",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "र्धस्य कदाचिदपि अधिकमर्धमपि बालत्ववृद्धत्वयोर्गतम्. According to our inter-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "pretation अपरम् would be used only to distinguish it from the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "first अर्धं but if so it might have been dispensed with. On",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "बालत्व and वृद्धत्व Râmarshi says बाल्यमविवेकेनेत्यर्थः तथा वृद्धत्वं कार्यासक्त्या",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "अवगणनयेत्यर्थः. व्याधिवियोगदुःख = the pains of illness and separation.—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. CVIII.—ब्रह्मज्ञानविवेकिनः = those who possess the discrimina-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "tion (i.e. between things real and unreal) which results from know-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "ledge of the Brahma. काञ्चन and धन together do not yield a good",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "reading. The reading of R. is thus explained उपभोगमुपयोगं भजन्ते",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "इत्येवंशीलानि (Râmarshi). भज् seems to mean here ‘affording.’",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "The meaning of the last two lines is clear but the construction",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "is not so, a number of relatives having to be supplied. This Stanza",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "occurs at p. 301 of the Kâvyasangraha.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. CIX.—परितर्जयन्ती—comp. Raghu IV., 28 and XI. 78., देहे",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "is a better reading than देहम् as the locative is the case com-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "monly employed with the root प्रहृ. अहितम् i. e. to oneself.—Va-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "santatilakâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. CX.—See Nîtis'ataka St. 92 note. पुरुषेषु रत्नं श्रेष्ठम्, according",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "to Râmarshi, which agrees with our interpretation. अहह Râmar-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "shi takes to be अद्भुते which will do as कष्टम् is खेदे.—S'ârdûla-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "vikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
